    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănĭm-aequus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		animus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>not easily moved;</i> also <i>of good
			courage</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animaequior esto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Bar. 4, 5, 21, 30</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib. Marc. 10, 49</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animaequiores estote filii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					Bar. 4, 27</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib.
				Sap. 18, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Act. 27, 36</span></i>.</div>
